            <h4 style="color: #002147; border-bottom: 2px solid #004080; padding-bottom: 5px; font-size:20px; font-weight:600;">About Er. Prashant Pathak</h4>
            <p style="font-size:16px; font-family:Arial; line-height:30px; text-align:justify; line-height:30px;color:black;">
                Er. Prashant Pathak is currently serving as an Assistant Professor at BRBBA Rajkiya Engineering College, Pratapgarh, with an academic background in Electronics Engineering. He is presently entrusted with key responsibilities as the Head of the Department of Computer Science & Engineering and also serves as the Officer In-charge/Coordinator for Scholarships at the institute. He is pursuing his Doctor of Philosophy (Ph.D.) from Madan Mohan Malaviya University of Technology (MMMUT), Gorakhpur, with a research focus in the area of Digital Electronics. He completed his M.Tech from Kamla Nehru Institute of Technology (KNIT), Sultanpur, specializing in Electronics Engineering. Er.Prashant Pathak has a keen interest in academic research and has published multiple papers in national and international journals and conferences. His recent research centers on the design of low-noise operational amplifiers for biomedical instrumentation, contributing to advancements in precision electronic systems for healthcare applications.
            </p>


